To style checkboxes, the best approach is to **visually hide** the native input and style its `<label>`:

```css
input[type="checkbox"] {
  position: absolute;
  opacity: 0;
}
label::before {
  content: " ";
  display: inline-block;
  width: 20px; height: 20px;
  border: 2px solid #333;
}
input:checked + label::before {
  background: #333;
}
```

The native input remains in the DOM, preserving all accessibility.
